# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows contributor with `core.autocrlf=true` — the default
# from the Git installer — checks every file out as CRLF while Biome's
# formatter expects LF. The result is a lint failure on files nobody touched,
# and a wall of "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every commit. `eol=lf` pins
# the checkout, so the same bytes land on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Lockfiles are generated; keep them out of diffs and reviews.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff

# Concurrent branches routinely append a bullet under the same `## YYYY-MM-DD`
# heading in the update history. A plain three-way merge conflicts on that
# shared context line even though the two edits do not overlap; the union
# merge driver instead keeps every line either side added, so both bullets
# land in the merged file with no manual resolution.
docs/log.md merge=union
